2. **Behavior added:** `-h` / `--no-filename` forces the filename prefix off regardless of the number of file operands. Combined short-option clusters (`-Hh`, `-hH`) are supported with left-to-right parsing.

3. **How last-one-wins is resolved:** A single tri-state variable `prefix_mode` (-1=unset, 0=off, 1=on) is set sequentially as options are parsed left-to-right. Each recognized option overwrites the previous value, so the last one seen wins. The final prefix decision is made once before any output: if `prefix_mode==1` prefix is on; if `prefix_mode==0` prefix is off; if `prefix_mode==-1` (neither given) the default rule applies (prefix when ≥2 files).

